A||||3||XDrewX||v8 info source ?||||1||
Z||000000||XDrewX||12-18-2001||11:39 PM||||I have aquired my V8 for my fiero, it is a SBC 350 4 bolt main.<P>Unfortunately thats about the extent of my knowledge on V8's. (except for the firing order, which I learned from Archie)<P>Anyway, where can find information about the 350 SBC, I would like to know things like:<BR>1. What the redline is?<BR>2. how much oil does it take?<BR>3. how much torque to apply to certain nuts and bolts.<BR>etc., etc.,  <BR> <BR>Is there a good book out there.<P>"350's for dummies"  LOL<P>thanks in advance<BR>peace, <P>DAP||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||12-19-2001||12:16 AM||||That all depends on which 350 you have.  Chevy made tons of different 350's, all with different redlines, etc.  Archie is a good source for the oil capacity, but until you know for sure, just fill it till the dipstick shows full.  Most 350's redline between 5000 and 6000 rpm, but hi perf models can wind much higher - depends on which one you have.<P>There's probably more info on the 350 Chevy engine than any other engine in the world.  Go to any bookstore and check out the automotive section.  If your engine came from a car, rather than a crate engine, get the manual for that car.  If it's a crate engine, GM should be able to supply you with the necessary info.||||reg||1
Z||000002||MrPAW||12-19-2001||09:06 AM||||I have used this book as a reference to rebuild half a dozen SBCs:  <A HREF="http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1557880298/qid=1008770111/sr=8-1/ref=sr_8_1_1/103-6081296-8008616" TARGET=_blank>http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1557880298/qid=1008770111/sr=8-1/ref=sr_8_1_1/103-6081296-8008616</A> <BR>It has all the torque specs, discusses differences between years and displacments of engines and in my opinion is a "must have" book for anyone starting with SBCs.<P>The same publishing company has a few books on performance mods but I have found that you can get just as much, and more up to date information from websites and excellent forums like this one.<P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000003||joplinfiero||12-19-2001||05:29 PM||||If you go to chevytalk.com they can help a great bunch of guys.. <P>Redline can be as high as the amount of money that you want to put in to the motor.. stock is about 5500.  The four bolt main can take a little more rpm.  <P>||||reg||1
